# The paths the owner merges (see CLAUDE.md, "Pull requests"). This file is the list. Once
# "Require review from Code Owners" is on in the protect-main ruleset (off today, see #135),
# GitHub enforces it, using the copy on the base branch. Until then .claude/hooks/merge_gate.py
# and the review rule enforce it: the hook refuses agent merges of the same paths, and
# test_merge_gate.py fails when a path here is not refused there.
# CLAUDE.md and .github/ are not listed (ordinary files since 2026-11-01). Lockfiles are not listed: CLAUDE.md lets the reviewer merge them by risk.
# (standard: one list that enforcement reads, with a test against drift, per policy-as-code
# guidance (vendor sources), checked 2026-11-01; departs from standard: the code-owner review
# setting is off for solo-fast speed, see #135.)
